<title>FRANCE: EDF-GDF to launch working hours talks - newspaper.</title>
<headline>EDF-GDF to launch working hours talks - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned utilities Electricite de France (EDF) and Gaz de France (GDF) plan to start negotiations with employees about shorter working hours as early as Monday, afternoon daily Le Monde said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Proposals will focus on introducing the 32-hour week and pay employees for 34 or 36 hours. The offer will be made to some 40,000 employees. EDF-GDF employees currently work a 38-hour week.</p>
<p>The plan would allow EDF-GDF to hire 13,000 additional workers over three years, Le Monde said.</p>
<p>Management is aiming for a speedy agreement in order to include the changes in working hours in the new contract EDF-GDF must sign with the state by end January.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
